<title>USA: Guaranty National Corp Q4 net, shr rise.</title>
<headline>Guaranty National Corp Q4 net, shr rise.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended  Twelve months ended</p>
<p>					    December 31,  December 31,</p>
<p>				     1996	1995     1996     1995</p>
<p>				 (In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p> Total revenues	     $138,890 $127,997 $529,542 $424,284</p>
<p>Operating earnings before</p>
<p>  realized gains		 7,048    2,166   23,788    6,790</p>
<p>Realized capital gains,</p>
<p>  net of tax		     1,925	257    5,496    2,139</p>
<p>Nonrecurring charge, net of tax</p>
<p>					 ---	---  (1,778)	---</p>
<p> Net earnings		    8,973    2,423   27,506    8,929</p>
<p>Average common shares and</p>
<p>share equivalents outstanding</p>
<p>				    14,982   14,720   14,973   13,324</p>
<p>Per share data:</p>
<p>Operating earnings before</p>
<p>  realized gains		  0.47     0.15     1.59     0.51</p>
<p>Realized capital gains,</p>
<p>  net of tax			0.13     0.01     0.37     0.16</p>
<p>Nonrecurring charge,</p>
<p>  net of tax			 ---	---   (0.12)	---</p>
<p> Net earnings		     0.60     0.16     1.84     0.67</p>
<p>NOTES: For Q4 1996, operating earnings were $7.0 million, or $0.47 per share, and after-tax realized capital gains were $1.9 million, or $0.13 per share.</p>
<p>For 1996, after-tax nonrecurring charge of $1.8 million, or $0.12 per share, was for expenses incurred when Orion Capital Corp made a tender offer which increased its ownership of the company's shares to 81 percent. After-tax realized capital gains were $5.5 million, or $0.37 cents per share.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
